{title: 184 - Jesus Paid It All}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Jesus Christ}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[Bm]I hear [D/A]the [A7]Savior say, "Thy [D/F#]strength indeed is small;
[D]Child of weakness, watch and pray, Find [A]in Me thine [F#m]all in all."
[F#m/A]Jesus paid it [D]all, All to Him I owe;
[A]Sin had left a [D/A]crimson [A7]stain, He washed it [D/F#]white as snow.

Refrain:
[D]Jesus paid it all,
[D]All to Him I owe;
[A]Sin had left a [D]crimson stain,
[D]He washed it white as [G/D]snow.

Verse 2:
[Bm]Lord, [D/A]now [A7/G]indeed [D/F#]I find
[D]Thy power and [A]Thine alone,
[F#m/A]Can change the [D]leper's spots
[A]And melt [D/A]the [A7/G]heart of [D/F#]stone.

Verse 3:
[Bm]Since [D/A]nothing [A7/G]good [D/F#]have I
[D]Whereby Thy [A]grace to [F#m]claim,
[F#m/A]I'll wash my [D]garments white
[A]In the [D/A]blood [A7]of Calv'ry's [D/F#]Lamb.

Verse 4:
[Bm]And [D/A]when [A7/G]before [D/F#]the throne
[D]I stand in Him [A]complete,
[F#m/A]I'll lay my [D]trophies down
[A]All down [D/A]at [A7/G]Jesus' [D/F#]feet.
